
Let's make the concept visual.

🔴 WITHOUT volatile

Suppose:

boolean running = true;

We have two threads.

                 SHARED VARIABLE
                  running = true
                       │
          ┌────────────┴────────────┐
          ↓                        	 ↓
      Thread 1                  	Thread 2
      reads true                	reads true
          │                        		 │
          │                    		changes it
          │                    	 running = false
          │                         	  │
          ↓                         	  ↓
    MAY STILL SEE                  	    false
       true
          │
          ↓
     Keeps running ❌

The important part:

Thread 2:
running = false
       ↓
Thread 1:
may still have/see old value = true

So Thread 1 may not immediately see the change.

🟢 WITH volatile

Now:

volatile boolean running = true;

Flow:

                  volatile variable
                   running = true
                        │
          ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
          ↓                            ↓
      Thread 1                  	  Thread 2
      reads true               	         reads true
          │                                  │
          │                     			 changes value
          │                      		running = false
          │                           		 │
          │                                  ↓
          │                            change is visible
          │                                  │
          └───────────────→ 		sees false
                                  	│
                                  	↓
                              	     stops ✅
The main difference

WITHOUT volatile:

Thread 2 changes
      ↓
running = false
      ↓
Thread 1 may see old value
      ↓
true ❌


WITH volatile:

Thread 2 changes
      ↓
running = false
      ↓
Thread 1 sees latest value
      ↓
false ✅
------------------------------